So i noticed that the answer will have $36a$, $4b$, $4c$, and $3d$ as exponents
and I thought lets use the A.M.-G.M. inequality on them\begin{align*}
\frac{ 36a + 4b + 4c + 3d}{4} &\geq \sqrt[4]{(36a)(4b)(4c)(3d)} \\
\frac{25}{4} &\geq \sqrt[4]{432a^2b^2cd} \\
\end{align*}
And that means that adding all the $a$ increases $f(a)$ by $1$, adding all the $b$ increases $f(b)$ by $1/2$, adding all the $c$ increases $f(c)$ by $1/3$, and adding all the $d$ increases $f(d)$ by $1/4$. Thus by the geometric mean theorem, the maximum value is when $f(b)=\frac{1}{2}$, $f(c)=\frac{1}{3}$, and $f(d)=\frac{1}{4}$. Seeing that $36 = 3*12$ to represent $1/a$, $4*2 = 8 = 2*b$, $4*0.75 = 3 = 3*c$, and $5/3 = 4*d$, we see that the answer to the problem is $12$ multiplied by all these values which equals to $180$.</think> <answer>180</answer>

